<title>USA: HIGH PRESSURE CONTINUES IN BRAZIL COFFEE BELT- WSC.</title>
<headline>HIGH PRESSURE CONTINUES IN BRAZIL COFFEE BELT- WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>High pressure along the coast of Brazil will promote mild days and cool nights across the coffee belt, Weather Services Corp said in an update Tuesday.</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies were observed in main growing areas of the belt this morning. Low temperatures ranged from 45-57 F (7-14 C). Some cooler conditions were reported in higher elevations.</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies are expected for the next seven days. Temperatures should stay near normal levels for this time of year. Low temperatures will range from the middle 40's to the 50's F (7-15 C).</p>
<p>&quot;There is no damaging cold expected,&quot; WSC said.</p>
<p>((Eileen Houlihan, New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640))</p>
